---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
// import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<Page
  title="Licenses and usage"
  description="Which licenses Dev Equip products use, and what that means for using them in your games."
>
  <h2>Licenses</h2>
  <p>Every product page lists the license that applies to it. Dev Equip uses two:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Designs, meshes and textures</strong> are released
      under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/deed.en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Creative Commons BY-NC-ND 4.0</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Source code</strong> is released under
      the <a href="https://github.com/Dev-Equip/Luau-Frameworks/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MIT License</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>When a product page shows both, each part of the product follows its own license.</p>

  <h2>Selling and redistributing</h2>
  <p>
    You can't sell any Dev Equip product. You can distribute products for free, as long as you follow the license shown
    on the product's page.
  </p>

  {/*
  <h2>Community products</h2>
  <p>
    Products marked <strong>Community</strong> are made by trusted developers outside Dev Equip, and their product page
    names who made them. They follow the license their developer gives, which is shown on the product's page.
  </p>
  <p>
    A paid community product is sold by its developer, through their own store. Dev Equip doesn't take part in the sale:
    your payment goes straight to the developer, and the developer is responsible for delivering the product, supporting
    it and handling refunds. If something goes wrong with a purchase, contact the developer or the store you bought it
    from first, and tell us if it isn't resolved so we can review the listing.
  </p>
  <p>
    Developers who want to list a project can read how it works on <a href={url('/sell/')}>Sell on Dev Equip</a>.
  </p>
  */}

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    If you're unsure whether something is allowed, ask in
    the <a href={SITE.discord} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Discord</a> before you use it.
  </p>
</Page>
